{UTF-8}
unit Prescriptions per person=
	1
	~	Rx/person
	~	Subscripts cannot have more than one unit, which leads to unit errors when \
		working with multiple projection input streams (Proj subscript). To \
		address this, we standardized the units of the projection inputs and end \
		values to dmnl; this constant (= 1) restores the units where the projected \
		value is used. This prevents unit errors and allows us to focus on \
		identifying and resolving actual model errors.
	|

unit Bup capacity estimated=
	1
	~	person
	~	Subscripts cannot have more than one unit, which leads to unit errors when \
		working with multiple projection input streams (Proj subscript). To \
		address this, we standardized the units of the projection inputs and end \
		values to dmnl; this constant (= 1) restores the units where the projected \
		value is used. This prevents unit errors and allows us to focus on \
		identifying and resolving actual model errors.
	|

unit MMT capacity estimated=
	1
	~	person
	~	Subscripts cannot have more than one unit, which leads to unit errors when \
		working with multiple projection input streams (Proj subscript). To \
		address this, we standardized the units of the projection inputs and end \
		values to dmnl; this constant (= 1) restores the units where the projected \
		value is used. This prevents unit errors and allows us to focus on \
		identifying and resolving actual model errors.
	|

unit Average days per prescription=
	1
	~	person*days/Rx
	~	Subscripts cannot have more than one unit, which leads to unit errors when \
		working with multiple projection input streams (Proj subscript). To \
		address this, we standardized the units of the projection inputs and end \
		values to dmnl; this constant (= 1) restores the units where the projected \
		value is used. This prevents unit errors and allows us to focus on \
		identifying and resolving actual model errors.
	|

unit Average MME per day=
	1
	~	MME/person/day
	~	Subscripts cannot have more than one unit, which leads to unit errors when \
		working with multiple projection input streams (Proj subscript). To \
		address this, we standardized the units of the projection inputs and end \
		values to dmnl; this constant (= 1) restores the units where the projected \
		value is used. This prevents unit errors and allows us to focus on \
		identifying and resolving actual model errors.
	|

unit Nx kits distributed net=
	1
	~	kits
	~	Subscripts cannot have more than one unit, which leads to unit errors when \
		working with multiple projection input streams (Proj subscript). To \
		address this, we standardized the units of the projection inputs and end \
		values to dmnl; this constant (= 1) restores the units where the projected \
