Effect of MOUD Tx on NonOD death rate[MMT]=
	0.37 ~~|
Effect of MOUD Tx on NonOD death rate[Bup]=
	0.54
	~	dmnl
	~	[LIT] Change in all-cause mortality, excepting overdose, attributable to \
		receipt of MOUD. While some studies do not find a statisticall significant \
		difference between buprenorphine and methadone, not all note this so we \
		have them separate. [Source: Degenhardt 2019, Ma 2018, Sordo 2017, Kelty \
		2017, Kelty 2018, Morgan 2019, Bahji 2019, Larochelle 2018] Canada: \
		Canadian estimates come from a few single studies with specific \
		populations or outcome definitions: MMT 0.72 (Nolan 2015, people who \
		inject drugs, Vancouver); 0.27 for non-external causes only (Russolillo \
		2018, people with criminal convictions, BC); about 0.57 MMT and 0.36 Bup \
		from crude non-drug-related death rates on vs off OAT (Pearce 2020, BC). \
		As they are broadly similar, the US SOURCE values, which draw on more \
		studies, are kept.
