	~	people/year
	~		|

Initiating Rx NP diverted base=
	362202
	~	people/year [100000,270000]
	~	[ACAL, DATA] Number of individuals initiating Rx NP use with diverted \
		opioids at model start. Canada: no Canadian initiation data, so the bounds \
		are derived from the US ratio of diverted initiates to past-year users \
		applied to Canadian users. US NSDUH 2008-09: about 12.3 million past-year \
		non-medical pain reliever users (4.84% of ages 12+); about 1.6-1.9 million \
		initiates per year from diverted sources (friend, relative or dealer \
		rather than own doctor), ratio 0.13-0.15. Canada 2009: 1,268,963 past-year \
		PWURx NP (Fischer et al. 2018; lower-upper 789,528-1,756,948) gives about \
		180,000 (range 100,000-270,000); population-scaled US value (1.88 million \
		x 0.11) is about 205,000. Calibration bounds: the US calibration range \
		(1.8-2.4 million) scaled by the Canada/US population aged 12+ in 2009 \
		(0.117) and widened (lower x0.5, upper x1.5): 105,300-421,200. Calibrated \
		value from Canada_main_MC.out. [US SOURCE: NSDUH RDAS]
	|

Initiating Rx NP diverted net  = 
        Initiating Rx NP diverted base 
             * ( 1
                  + RAMP ( Policy change initiating Rx NP diverted 
                            / Policy rampup duration , 
                       Policy activation time , 
                       Policy activation time 
                            + Policy rampup duration ) )
	~	people/year
	~	Number of individuals initiating Rx NP use with diverted opioids at model \
		start, accounting for policy changes going forward after the MaxDataTime. \
		Conceptually, this figure represents the 'base rate' of initiation, \
		similar to base fractional rates.
	|

