Net quitting heroin with Rx NP=
	Nondisordered heroin use * MIN( Max per capita flow rate, Net quit rate heroin with Rx NP\
		 * Perceived risk coeff net quit NDHU with Rx )
	~	people/year
	~	Individuals with NDHU and Rx NP use who quit heroin use, net of \
		resumptions. Per-capita rate capped at Max per capita flow rate (numerical \
		safeguard; see that variable).
	|

Max per capita flow rate=
	4
	~	1/year
	~	Numerical safeguard: upper limit on the per-capita rate of the stock- \
		proportional flows that are multiplied by perceived-risk, social- \
		influence or availability coefficients (initiating heroin, developing Rx \
		OUD or HUD, net quitting). With TIME STEP = 0.0625 year, total outflow \
		rates above 16 per year empty a stock in less than one step and make it \
		negative (Euler overshoot); this happened in extreme calibration trials \
		(e.g. net quitting heroin with Rx OUD reaching 35-40 per year when \
		perceived risk relative was about 11 and its strength about 2). 4 per year \
		(mean time in the state 3 months) keeps the sum of these outflows below \
		1/TIME STEP; in the calibrated runs these rates stay below 1 per year, so \
		the cap does not change them.
	|

Net quitting heroin with Rx OUD=
	Rx OUD with PY heroin no MOUD * MIN( Max per capita flow rate, Net quit rate heroin with Rx OUD\
		 * Perceived risk coeff net quit heroin with Rx OUD )
	~	people/year
	~	Individuals with Rx OUD and heroin use who quit use of heroin, net of \
		resumptions. Per-capita rate capped at Max per capita flow rate (numerical \
		safeguard; see that variable).
	|

Net quitting NDHU=
	Nondisordered heroin use * MIN( Max per capita flow rate, Net quit rate NDHU * Perceived risk coeff net quit NDHU\
		 * Heroin availability coeff net quit NDHU )
	~	people/year
	~	Per-capita rate capped at Max per capita flow rate (numerical safeguard; \
		see that variable).
	|

Net quitting Rx NP=
	PWURx NP no PY heroin * MIN( Max per capita flow rate, Net quit rate Rx NP * Perceived risk coeff net quit Rx NP\
		 * Rx availability coeff net quit Rx NP )
	~	people/year
	~	PWURx-NP who quit that use. Stock and initiation flows are grounded in \
		data, so this lets us better estimate net resumptoin-quit rates (applies \
		to NP use to NP heroin) and to Rx OUD with vs without PY heroin Per-capita \
		rate capped at Max per capita flow rate (numerical safeguard; see that \
		variable).
	|

