	|

Rx demand Rx NP  = 2000
	~	MME/person/year [0,5000,500]
	~	[DATA, ASM] Demand for Rx opioids by PWURx-NP. We use frequency data from \
		NSDUH  combined with assumed MMEs consumed per day of use. [Source: NSDUH \
		2010-18]
	|

Rx demand Rx OUD no H=
	11000
	~	MME/person/year [0,20000,1000]
	~	[DATA, ASM] Demand for Rx opioids by individuals with Rx OUD and no heroin \
		use. We use frequency data from NSDUH combined with assumed MMEs consumed \
		per day of use. [Source: NSDUH 2010-18]
	|

Rx demand Rx OUD with H=
	18000
	~	MME/person/year [0,30000,1000]
	~	[DATA, ASM] Demand for Rx opioids by individuals with Rx OUD + heroin use. \
		We use frequency data from NSDUH  combined with assumed MMEs consumed per \
		day of use. [Source: NSDUH 2010-18]
	|

PWURx NP no PY heroin  = 
        INTEG( Initiating Rx NP diverted 
                  + Initiating Rx NP own Rx 
                  - Developing Rx OUD 
                  - Initiating heroin with Rx NP 
                  - Net quitting Rx NP 
                  + Net quitting heroin with Rx NP 
                  - NonOD death Rx NP 
                  - Overdose death Rx NP , 
             Initial PWURx NP no H )
	~	people [?,1.1e+07]
	~		|

Rx OUD all total  = 
        Rx OUD no PY heroin total 
             + Rx OUD with PY heroin total
	~	person
	~		|

Rx OUD no heroin by MOUD[TxT]  = 
        INTEG( Tx engagement Rx OUD no H[TxT] 
                  - Tx exit in remission Rx OUD no H[TxT] 
                  - Tx exit with UD Rx OUD no H[TxT] 
                  - NonOD death Rx OUD no H in Tx[TxT] 
                  - Overdose death Rx OUD no H in Tx[TxT] , 
             Initial Rx OUD no H in Tx[TxT] )
	~	people
	~		|

Rx OUD no PY heroin no MOUD  = 
        INTEG( Developing Rx OUD 
                  + Net quitting heroin with Rx OUD 
                  - Initiating heroin with Rx OUD 
                  - Remitting Rx OUD no H no MOUD Tx 
                  - NonOD death Rx OUD no H 
                  - Overdose death Rx OUD no H 
                  + Relapsing to Rx OUD no H 
                  + SUM ( Tx exit with UD Rx OUD no H[TxT!] 
                            - Tx engagement Rx OUD no H[TxT!] ) , 
             Initial Rx OUD no H )
	~	people [?,4e+06]
	~		|

Rx OUD with heroin by MOUD[TxT]  = 
        INTEG( Tx engagement Rx OUD with H[TxT] 
                  - Tx exit in remission Rx OUD with H[TxT] 
                  - Tx exit with UD Rx OUD with H[TxT] 
                  - NonOD death Rx OUD with H in Tx[TxT] 
                  - Overdose death Rx OUD with H in Tx[TxT] , 
             Initial Rx OUD with H in Tx[TxT] )
	~	people
	~		|

Rx OUD with PY heroin no MOUD  = 
        INTEG( Initiating heroin with Rx OUD 
                  - Developing HUD with Rx OUD 
                  - Net quitting heroin with Rx OUD 
                  - Remitting Rx OUD with H no MOUD Tx 
                  - NonOD death Rx OUD with H 
                  - Overdose death Rx OUD with H 
                  + Relapsing to Rx OUD with H 
                  + SUM ( Tx exit with UD Rx OUD with H[TxT!] 
                            - Tx engagement Rx OUD with H[TxT!] ) , 
             Initial Rx OUD with H )
	~	people [?,200000]
	~		|

Rx street supply disruption  = 
        INTEG( Rx street supply shocks 
                  - Rx street supply readjustment , 
             0)
	~	dmnl
	~	Abstract stock representing temporary disruptions to the street / diverted \
		Rx supply, such as withdrawal of a preferred drug from the market. Street \
		supply eventually readjusts to meet demand with whatever opioids are \
		available, but temporary disruptions will have a short- to medium-term \
		impact on street Rx prices.
	|

Rx street supply readjustment  = 
        Rx street supply disruption 
             / Time to readjust Rx street supply
	~	1/year
	~	Represents the process of gradual readjustment of street supply to \
		prevailing conditions in response to disruptions
	|

Rx supply relative net  = 
        Rx supply relative 
             * ( 1
                  + RAMP ( Policy change Rx supply relative 
                            / Policy rampup duration , 
                       Policy activation time , 
                       Policy activation time 
                            + Policy rampup duration ) )
	~	dmnl
	~	Supply of prescription opioids available for potential NP use, indexed to \
		model initiation, after accounting for policy changes.
	|

Rx vs H availability coeff developing HUD with Rx OUD=
	Rx vs heroin availability index 
	             ^ (- Rx vs H availability strength developing HUD with Rx OUD)
	~	dmnl
	~	The multiplier effect of the relative price of Rx opioids compared to \
		heroin (relative to their respective prices at model initiation) on \
		developing an HUD among people who have an Rx OUD.
	|

Rx vs H availability coeff initiating heroin with Rx OUD=
	Rx vs heroin availability index 
	             ^ (- Rx vs H availability strength initiating heroin with Rx OUD)
	~	dmnl
	~	The multiplier effect of the relative price of Rx opioids compared to \
		heroin (relative to their respective prices at model initiation) on \
		initiating nondisordered heroin use among people who have an Rx OUD.
	|

Rx vs H availability strength developing HUD with Rx OUD = 1.26477
	~	dmnl [0,2]
	~	[ACAL] Sensitivity of development of HUD in individuals who have an Rx OUD \
		to the relative price of Rx vs Heroin (relative to their respective prices \
		at model start (INITAL TIME)).
	|

Rx vs H availability strength initiating heroin with Rx OUD = 1e-06
	~	dmnl [0,2,0.05]
	~	[ACAL] Sensitivity of initiation of heroin use in individuals who have Rx \
		OUD to the relative price of Rx vs Heroin (relative to their respective \
		prices at model start (INITAL TIME)).
	|

Rx vs H availability strength initiating NDHU with Rx = 0.18897
	~	dmnl [0,2,0.05]
	~	[ACAL] Sensitivity of initiation of heroin use in PWURx-NP to the relative \
		price of Rx vs Heroin (relative to their respective prices at model start \
		(INITAL TIME)).
	|

Sensitivity of Rx supply to MME per day  = 1
	~	dmnl [0,2]
	~	[ASM] Weight parameter determining the relative importance of prescription \
		strengths (MME/day) vs. number of people with opioid prescriptions in \
		affecting the supply of 'excess' Rx available for NP use. A value of 1 is \
		neutral, giving equal importance to size & number. A values less than 1 \
		indicates that diversion is driven more by the number of people with a \
		prescription, while a value greater than 1 indicates diversion is driven \
		more by the strength of presriptions.
	|

SI on developing HUD current  = 
        Effective SI HUD development 
             / Population
	~	dmnl
	~	Current Social Influence impact on the development of HUD.
	|

SI on developing HUD reference  = 
        INITIAL( SI on developing HUD current  )
	~	dmnl
	~	Social Influence impact on the development of HUD at model initiation \
		(INITIAL TIME).
	|

SI on developing HUD relative  = 
        SI on developing HUD current 
             / SI on developing HUD reference
	~	dmnl
	~	Current Social Influence impact on the development of HUD relative to \
		model initiation (INITIAL TIME).
	|

SI on developing Rx OUD current  = 
        Effective SI Rx OUD development 
             / Population
	~	dmnl
