	~		|

Policy rampup duration=
	3
	~	year [?,10]
	~		|

Policy change social influence strength relapse=
	0
	~	dmnl [-2,2,0.01]
	~	Functions as a direct input to the social-influence (peer recovery) \
		strength on relapse, not as a % change, because that strength is zero by \
		default (no peer-recovery loop at baseline). Relapse flows are multiplied \
		by Social influence coefficient relapse = SI on remission relative ^ \
		(-strength). For the Canadian analysis, the strength was set so that this \
		multiplier equals 0.9, 0.8 and 0.5 (a 10%, 20% and 50% reduction in \
		relapse) at the end of the ramp-up period (2029), consistent with the \
		other policy levers: 0.138 (10%), 0.293 (20%), 0.911 (50%) \
		(PeerRecovery10/20/50.cin). Values were derived under the base projection \
		scenario with the calibrated parameters (Canada_main_MC.out), using SI on \
		remission relative in 2029 from PeerRecovery_check.cmd (2.140); strength = \
		-ln(multiplier) / ln(SI on remission relative 2029).
	|

