		only. No Canadian estimate is available, so the US estimate (866,830, for \
		1999) was scaled to Canada (using the ratio of the Canadian to US \
		population in 1999) to give a plausible order of magnitude. The initial \
		stock built from this value is multiplied by the calibrated Initial stock \
		correction[OUS] (Canada_main_MC.out), so the starting stock is effectively \
