	~	dmnl [0,1]
	~	[DATA] Canada: 0.115 = past-month heroin use (self-report) among 492 \
		methadone patients in 13 Ontario clinics [Source: Bawor et al. 2015, \
		Biology of Sex Differences]. No direct Canadian split by use disorder was \
		found. Before 2014 most Canadian MOUD patients were treated for \
		prescription-opioid dependence, so the US value does not apply. The same \
		value is used for methadone and buprenorphine. The rest of the initial \
		MOUD patients are Rx OUD (with PY heroin: 0.0048, US value; without: the \
		remainder). [US SOURCE: TEDSA 1999, value 0.96: fraction of all planned \
		MAT episodes for a primary substance of heroin, Rx opioids or non-Rx \
		methadone where heroin was the primary or only substance named; assumed \
		MMT was the only MOUD being planned]
	|

